\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Task A pairwise duplicate detection for all six models under four post-processing settings. For every model and method we select one layer by training-set AUROC and report the test-set numbers at that layer; the subscript gives the selected layer. ABTT uses $D$ tuned on train. Baseline AUROC spans 0.839 to 0.970 across the six models, and ABTT lifts every model into a 0.971 to 0.984 band. Cosine gap is the mean same-directory cosine minus the mean different-directory cosine. Per-layer grids are in Appendix Tables~\ref {tab:taskA_main} and~\ref {tab:taskA_appendix}, and the SIF sweeps in Appendix Table~\ref {tab:taskA_appendix_sif}.}}{6}{table.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:taskA_headline}{{2}{6}{Task A pairwise duplicate detection for all six models under four post-processing settings. For every model and method we select one layer by training-set AUROC and report the test-set numbers at that layer; the subscript gives the selected layer. ABTT uses $D$ tuned on train. Baseline AUROC spans 0.839 to 0.970 across the six models, and ABTT lifts every model into a 0.971 to 0.984 band. Cosine gap is the mean same-directory cosine minus the mean different-directory cosine. Per-layer grids are in Appendix Tables~\ref {tab:taskA_main} and~\ref {tab:taskA_appendix}, and the SIF sweeps in Appendix Table~\ref {tab:taskA_appendix_sif}}{table.caption.12}{}}
