\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Task A AUROC against normalized layer depth for all six models. The three T5 encoders in the top row lose almost all pairwise separation in their middle layers, with LaTa reaching chance. The three sentence-embedding models in the bottom row improve close to monotonically with depth and never dip below 0.80. ABTT holds every model near its ceiling at every depth, so the repair does not depend on the collapse being present.}}{7}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dip}{{2}{7}{Task A AUROC against normalized layer depth for all six models. The three T5 encoders in the top row lose almost all pairwise separation in their middle layers, with LaTa reaching chance. The three sentence-embedding models in the bottom row improve close to monotonically with depth and never dip below 0.80. ABTT holds every model near its ceiling at every depth, so the repair does not depend on the collapse being present}{figure.caption.14}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Cosine gap against normalized layer depth for all six models. The baseline gap stays under 0.29 at every layer of every model, and under 0.11 at every layer of Qwen3-0.6B, so raw cosine carries almost no decision margin anywhere. ABTT lifts all six models to a gap near 0.5 across the whole depth profile. SIF raises the gap for LaTa and PhilTa and leaves the remaining four models close to baseline.}}{7}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gap}{{3}{7}{Cosine gap against normalized layer depth for all six models. The baseline gap stays under 0.29 at every layer of every model, and under 0.11 at every layer of Qwen3-0.6B, so raw cosine carries almost no decision margin anywhere. ABTT lifts all six models to a gap near 0.5 across the whole depth profile. SIF raises the gap for LaTa and PhilTa and leaves the remaining four models close to baseline}{figure.caption.15}{}}
